IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `coq-common`
IMPORT `coq-deaths`

-- Coroners Act 2003 (Queensland) -- worked cases for coq-common.l4 (family member) and coq-deaths.l4 (ss 7-12, 11A).
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Expected values were written by hand
-- from the deposited text (act-2003-013, in force from 2026-10-29), never copied from the encoding's output. No scenario
-- life raised this Act; the facts are the encoder's, HYPOTHETICAL throughout. Every "considers", "is satisfied" and
-- "reasonably believes" of an official is given as a fact.
--
-- Unofficial version. Based on content from the Queensland Legislation website at 6 November 2026. (c) The State of
-- Queensland, CC BY 4.0. See SOURCE-LICENSE.md.
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

GIVEN d IS A NUMBER, m IS A NUMBER, y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`dmy` d m y MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY d m y

§ `Schedule 2 -- family member`

-- The spouse comes first whatever else is true.
#ASSERT `Am I the family member` FALSE FALSE `spouse (including a de facto partner)` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: as spouse (sch 2, family member, paragraph (b)(i))`
-- An adult child, while a spouse is reasonably available: not yet.
#ASSERT `Am I the family member` FALSE FALSE `adult child` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: someone ahead of you in paragraph (b) is reasonably available`
-- An adult child of a widower (no spouse exists, so none is reasonably available).
#ASSERT `Am I the family member` FALSE FALSE `adult child` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: as an adult child, no spouse being reasonably available (paragraph (b)(ii))`
-- A parent, while an adult child is available.
#ASSERT `Am I the family member` FALSE FALSE `parent` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: someone ahead of you in paragraph (b) is reasonably available`
-- A parent of a young unmarried worker with no children.
#ASSERT `Am I the family member` FALSE FALSE `parent` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: as a parent, no spouse or adult child being reasonably available (paragraph (b)(iii))`
-- A sibling, while a parent is available; and when the parents are dead.
#ASSERT `Am I the family member` FALSE FALSE `adult brother or sister` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: someone ahead of you in paragraph (b) is reasonably available`
#ASSERT `Am I the family member` FALSE FALSE `adult brother or sister` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: as an adult sibling, no spouse, adult child or parent being reasonably available (paragraph (b)(iv))`
-- A close friend: only when none of the four is available, and only if the coroner considers the relationship sufficient.
#ASSERT `Am I the family member` FALSE FALSE `another adult with a close relationship immediately before the death` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `yes: as an adult the coroner considers had a sufficient relationship, no spouse, adult child, parent or adult sibling being reasonably available (paragraph (b)(v))`
#ASSERT `Am I the family member` FALSE FALSE `another adult with a close relationship immediately before the death` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: the definition of family member does not include you`
#ASSERT `Am I the family member` FALSE FALSE `another adult with a close relationship immediately before the death` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `no: someone ahead of you in paragraph (b) is reasonably available`
-- An ATSI family member: needs the deceased to have been Aboriginal or Torres Strait Islander.
#ASSERT `Am I the family member` FALSE FALSE `an appropriate person under the tradition or custom of the deceased's Aboriginal or Torres Strait Islander community` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `yes: as an ATSI family member, no spouse, adult child, parent or adult sibling being reasonably available (paragraph (b)(vi))`
#ASSERT `Am I the family member` FALSE FALSE `an appropriate person under the tradition or custom of the deceased's Aboriginal or Torres Strait Islander community` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: the definition of family member does not include you`
#ASSERT `Am I the family member` FALSE FALSE `an appropriate person under the tradition or custom of the deceased's Aboriginal or Torres Strait Islander community` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `no: someone ahead of you in paragraph (b) is reasonably available`
-- Paragraph (a): a document naming a friend (an attorney under an advance health directive) displaces paragraph (b).
#ASSERT `Am I the family member` TRUE FALSE `none of these` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: a document satisfied the coroner that the deceased wished you to be the family member (sch 2, family member, paragraph (a))`
#ASSERT `Am I the family member` FALSE TRUE `spouse (including a de facto partner)` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: the deceased's documented wish named someone else as the family member (paragraph (a))`
#ASSERT `Am I the family member` FALSE FALSE `none of these` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: the definition of family member does not include you`
#ASSERT (`sch 2 -- family member` FALSE FALSE `parent` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE) `makes me a family member`
#ASSERT NOT ((`sch 2 -- family member` FALSE FALSE `parent` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE) `makes me a family member`)

§ `s 8 -- reportable death`

-- Argument order: where, body in Qld, lived in Qld, journey, event in Qld, reported outside, VAD, identity unknown,
-- injury, otherwise unnatural, suspicious, health care, independent person would not expect, no certificate, care,
-- custody, authority, police operations.
-- A natural death at home in Brisbane, certificate issued: not reportable.
#ASSERT `Is the death reportable question` `in Queensland` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `no injury played a part` FALSE FALSE `health care played no such part` FALSE FALSE `none of these` `not in, escaping from or avoiding custody` `no detention` FALSE EQUALS `no: the death is none of the kinds s 8(3) lists`
-- A worker crushed at a Brisbane site and killed: injury caused the death (s 8A(a)).
#ASSERT `Is the death reportable question` `in Queensland` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `an injury caused the death` FALSE FALSE `health care played no such part` FALSE FALSE `none of these` `not in, escaping from or avoiding custody` `no detention` FALSE EQUALS `yes: the death is a reportable death (s 8)`
-- A road crash victim who dies months later; the injury contributed and without it they would not have died (s 8A(b)).
#ASSERT `Is the death reportable question` `in Queensland` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `an injury contributed to the death, and without it the person would not have died` FALSE FALSE `health care played no such part` FALSE FALSE `none of these` `not in, escaping from or avoiding custody` `no detention` FALSE EQUALS `yes: the death is a reportable death (s 8)`
-- An injury that contributed, but the person would have died anyway: s 8A does not reach it, and nothing else is shown.
#ASSERT `Is the death reportable question` `in Queensland` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `an injury contributed to the death, but the person would have died anyway` FALSE FALSE `health care played no such part` FALSE FALSE `none of these` `not in, escaping from or avoiding custody` `no detention` FALSE EQUALS `no: the death is none of the kinds s 8(3) lists`
-- A death in New South Wales of a NSW resident, no Queensland link: s 8(2) fails.
#ASSERT `Is the death reportable question` `elsewhere in Australia` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `an injury caused the death` FALSE FALSE `health care played no such part` FALSE FALSE `none of these` `not in, escaping from or avoiding custody` `no detention` FALSE EQUALS `no: the death has none of the connections with Queensland s 8(2) requires`
-- A Queenslander killed in NSW, reported to the NSW coroner: s 8(4).
#ASSERT `Is the death reportable question` `elsewhere in Australia` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE `an injury caused the death` FALSE FALSE `health care played no such part` FALSE FALSE `none of these` `not in, escaping from or avoiding custody` `no detention` FALSE EQUALS `no: the death happened outside Queensland and has been reported to a coroner there (s 8(4))`
-- The same death not reported to a coroner there: reportable (s 8(2)(b)(ii)).
#ASSERT `Is the death reportable question` `elsewhere in Australia` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `an injury caused the death` FALSE FALSE `health care played no such part` FALSE FALSE `none of these` `not in, escaping from or avoiding custody` `no detention` FALSE EQUALS `yes: the death is a reportable death (s 8)`
-- A death overseas, body brought home to Queensland, violent: reportable (s 8(2)(b)(i)).
#ASSERT `Is the death reportable question` `outside Australia` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `no injury played a part` TRUE FALSE `health care played no such part` FALSE FALSE `none of these` `not in, escaping from or avoiding custody` `no detention` FALSE EQUALS `yes: the death is a reportable death (s 8)`
-- A traveller on the way to Queensland; and a death outside caused by an event in Queensland.
#ASSERT `Is the death reportable question` `elsewhere in Australia` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `no injury played a part` FALSE TRUE `health care played no such part` FALSE FALSE `none of these` `not in, escaping from or avoiding custody` `no detention` FALSE EQUALS `yes: the death is a reportable death (s 8)`
#ASSERT `Is the death reportable question` `elsewhere in Australia` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE `an injury caused the death` FALSE FALSE `health care played no such part` FALSE FALSE `none of these` `not in, escaping from or avoiding custody` `no detention` FALSE EQUALS `yes: the death is a reportable death (s 8)`
-- Voluntary assisted dying: not reportable, despite anything else (s 8(5)).
#ASSERT `Is the death reportable question` `in Queensland` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE `no injury played a part` TRUE FALSE `health care played no such part` FALSE TRUE `none of these` `not in, escaping from or avoiding custody` `no detention` FALSE EQUALS `no: the death was a voluntary assisted death (s 8(5))`
-- Health care: surgery that caused a death an independent person would not have expected; and one they would have.
#ASSERT `Is the death reportable question` `in Queensland` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `no injury played a part` FALSE FALSE `health care the person received caused, or is likely to have caused, the death` TRUE FALSE `none of these` `not in, escaping from or avoiding custody` `no detention` FALSE EQUALS `yes: the death is a reportable death (s 8)`
#ASSERT `Is the death reportable question` `in Queensland` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `no injury played a part` FALSE FALSE `health care the person received caused, or is likely to have caused, the death` FALSE FALSE `none of these` `not in, escaping from or avoiding custody` `no detention` FALSE EQUALS `no: the death is none of the kinds s 8(3) lists`
-- A failure to provide care that was sought (s 10AA(2)).
#ASSERT `Is the death reportable question` `in Queensland` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `no injury played a part` FALSE FALSE `health care was sought but not provided, and the failure contributed, or is likely to have contributed, to the death (had it been provided the person would not have died when they did)` TRUE FALSE `none of these` `not in, escaping from or avoiding custody` `no detention` FALSE EQUALS `yes: the death is a reportable death (s 8)`
-- Identity unknown; suspicious; no certificate likely; police operations.
#ASSERT `Is the death reportable question` `in Queensland` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE `no injury played a part` FALSE FALSE `health care played no such part` FALSE FALSE `none of these` `not in, escaping from or avoiding custody` `no detention` FALSE EQUALS `yes: the death is a reportable death (s 8)`
#ASSERT `Is the death reportable question` `in Queensland` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `no injury played a part` FALSE TRUE `health care played no such part` FALSE FALSE `none of these` `not in, escaping from or avoiding custody` `no detention` FALSE EQUALS `yes: the death is a reportable death (s 8)`
#ASSERT `Is the death reportable question` `in Queensland` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `no injury played a part` FALSE FALSE `health care played no such part` FALSE TRUE `none of these` `not in, escaping from or avoiding custody` `no detention` FALSE EQUALS `yes: the death is a reportable death (s 8)`
#ASSERT `Is the death reportable question` `in Queensland` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `no injury played a part` FALSE FALSE `health care played no such part` FALSE FALSE `none of these` `not in, escaping from or avoiding custody` `no detention` TRUE EQUALS `yes: the death is a reportable death (s 8)`
-- Care: a child in foster care under the chief executive's custody who dies of illness in hospital (s 9(1)(d), (3)).
#ASSERT `Is the death reportable question` `in Queensland` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `no injury played a part` FALSE FALSE `health care played no such part` FALSE FALSE `(d) a child in the chief executive's custody or guardianship, placed under an assessment care agreement, or under a child protection order giving custody or long-term guardianship to someone other than a parent` `not in, escaping from or avoiding custody` `no detention` FALSE EQUALS `yes: the death is a reportable death (s 8)`
-- Custody: a prisoner held under a court order dies of natural causes; a person detained only under the Mental Health
-- Act 2016 is not in "custody" (s 10(2)(c)(ii)); a driver fleeing arrest by Commonwealth officers; no detention at all.
#ASSERT `Is the death reportable question` `in Queensland` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `no injury played a part` FALSE FALSE `health care played no such part` FALSE FALSE `none of these` `in custody` `a court order` FALSE EQUALS `yes: the death is a reportable death (s 8)`
#ASSERT `Is the death reportable question` `in Queensland` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `no injury played a part` FALSE FALSE `health care played no such part` FALSE FALSE `none of these` `in custody` `the Education (General Provisions) Act 2006, the Mental Health Act 2016 or the Forensic Disability Act 2011 only` FALSE EQUALS `no: the death is none of the kinds s 8(3) lists`
#ASSERT `Is the death reportable question` `in Queensland` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `no injury played a part` FALSE FALSE `health care played no such part` FALSE FALSE `none of these` `trying to avoid being put into custody` `an Act of the Commonwealth` FALSE EQUALS `yes: the death is a reportable death (s 8)`
#ASSERT `Is the death reportable question` `in Queensland` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `no injury played a part` FALSE FALSE `health care played no such part` FALSE FALSE `none of these` `not in, escaping from or avoiding custody` `an arrest` FALSE EQUALS `no: the death is none of the kinds s 8(3) lists`

§ `s 7 -- must I report the death`

-- Argument order: aware of an apparently reportable death, believe someone else reported it, relevant service provider,
-- care, police operations, death in custody.
#ASSERT `Must I report the death question` FALSE FALSE FALSE `none of these` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: s 7 does not require you to report it, as you are not aware of a death that appears to be reportable; you may still report it if you consider it may be reportable (s 7(7))`
-- A co-worker finds a colleague dead after a fall at work; no one else has called anyone.
#ASSERT `Must I report the death question` TRUE FALSE FALSE `none of these` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: report it immediately to a police officer or a coroner (s 7(3)(c)); maximum penalty 25 penalty units`
-- The same, but the co-worker sees the ambulance officers ring the police.
#ASSERT `Must I report the death question` TRUE TRUE FALSE `none of these` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: s 7 does not require you to report it, as you reasonably believe someone else has reported or is reporting it; you may still report it (s 7(7))`
-- The provider of a level 3 residential service must report whatever it believes (s 7(2)).
#ASSERT `Must I report the death question` TRUE TRUE TRUE `(a) a person with a disability living in a level 3 accredited residential service, a department-funded disability accommodation service, or a health-funded residential service that is not a private dwelling or aged care facility` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: report it immediately to a police officer or a coroner (s 7(3)(c)); maximum penalty 25 penalty units`
#ASSERT `Must I report the death question` TRUE TRUE TRUE `(f) not living in a private dwelling or aged care facility, receiving services under the Commonwealth's Disability Support for Older Australians Program or another prescribed Commonwealth program` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `yes: report it immediately to the State Coroner or a Deputy State Coroner (s 7(3)(a) or (b)); maximum penalty 25 penalty units`
-- s 7(2) does not reach head (b) (mental health), nor a person who is not the provider.
#ASSERT `Must I report the death question` TRUE TRUE TRUE `(b) an involuntary patient detained in or being transported to or from an authorised mental health service, on supervised limited community treatment or absence, or detained under an emergency examination authority` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: s 7 does not require you to report it, as you reasonably believe someone else has reported or is reporting it; you may still report it (s 7(7))`
#ASSERT `Must I report the death question` TRUE TRUE FALSE `(e) an NDIS participant not living in a private dwelling or aged care facility, receiving a relevant class of supports from a registered NDIS provider` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: s 7 does not require you to report it, as you reasonably believe someone else has reported or is reporting it; you may still report it (s 7(7))`
-- Police operations; a death in custody.
#ASSERT `Must I report the death question` TRUE FALSE FALSE `none of these` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `yes: report it immediately to the State Coroner or a Deputy State Coroner (s 7(3)(a) or (b)); maximum penalty 25 penalty units`
#ASSERT `Must I report the death question` TRUE FALSE FALSE `none of these` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `yes: report it immediately to the State Coroner or a Deputy State Coroner (s 7(3)(a) or (b)); maximum penalty 25 penalty units`

§ `ss 11, 12(1) -- must a coroner investigate`

#ASSERT `Must a coroner investigate question` `in Queensland` FALSE TRUE FALSE `no direction` EQUALS `yes: a coroner must investigate, considering the death reportable (s 11(2))`
#ASSERT `Must a coroner investigate question` `in Queensland` FALSE TRUE TRUE `no direction` EQUALS `no new investigation: another coroner is already investigating the death (s 11(2)(b))`
#ASSERT `Must a coroner investigate question` `in Queensland` FALSE FALSE FALSE `no direction` EQUALS `no: a coroner may investigate only a death the coroner considers reportable, or one directed (s 11(2), (3))`
#ASSERT `Must a coroner investigate question` `in Queensland` FALSE FALSE FALSE `the State Coroner directed it, considering the death reportable (s 11(4)(a))` EQUALS `yes: a coroner must investigate, because of a direction (s 11(3), s 12(1))`
-- A Queenslander killed overseas: no investigation without the Minister (s 12(1)(b)), even if the State Coroner directs
-- under s 11(4)(a).
#ASSERT `Must a coroner investigate question` `outside Australia` FALSE TRUE FALSE `no direction` EQUALS `no: a coroner must not investigate a death outside Australia, or in another State and reported to a coroner there, without the Minister's direction (s 12(1))`
#ASSERT `Must a coroner investigate question` `outside Australia` FALSE TRUE FALSE `the State Coroner directed it, considering the death reportable (s 11(4)(a))` EQUALS `no: a coroner must not investigate a death outside Australia, or in another State and reported to a coroner there, without the Minister's direction (s 12(1))`
#ASSERT `Must a coroner investigate question` `outside Australia` FALSE FALSE FALSE `the Minister directed it, or the State Coroner directed it on the Minister's direction (s 11(4)(b))` EQUALS `yes: a coroner must investigate, because of a direction (s 11(3), s 12(1))`
-- A death in NSW: barred once reported to the NSW coroner, not before.
#ASSERT `Must a coroner investigate question` `elsewhere in Australia` TRUE TRUE FALSE `no direction` EQUALS `no: a coroner must not investigate a death outside Australia, or in another State and reported to a coroner there, without the Minister's direction (s 12(1))`
#ASSERT `Must a coroner investigate question` `elsewhere in Australia` FALSE TRUE FALSE `no direction` EQUALS `yes: a coroner must investigate, considering the death reportable (s 11(2))`
#ASSERT `Must a coroner investigate question` `elsewhere in Australia` TRUE FALSE FALSE `the Minister directed it, or the State Coroner directed it on the Minister's direction (s 11(4)(b))` EQUALS `yes: a coroner must investigate, because of a direction (s 11(3), s 12(1))`

§ `ss 11(7), 11AAA -- which coroner`

-- Argument order: violent or unnatural, injury, mining or petroleum injury, where received, self-inflicted, custody,
-- police operations.
-- A miner killed by a roof fall at an underground coal mine.
#ASSERT `Which coroner investigates question` TRUE `an injury caused the death` TRUE `at a coal mine` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the Mining and Resources Coroner, or if that coroner is not available another coroner the State Coroner directs (s 11AAA(1))`
-- A gas field worker whose burns contributed to a death that would not otherwise have happened.
#ASSERT `Which coroner investigates question` TRUE `an injury contributed to the death, and without it the person would not have died` TRUE `at or in a petroleum and gas site` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the Mining and Resources Coroner, or if that coroner is not available another coroner the State Coroner directs (s 11AAA(1))`
-- Intentionally self-inflicted at a mine; an injury that contributed but without which the person would still have
-- died; an injury not from mining operations; an injury away from a mine.
#ASSERT `Which coroner investigates question` TRUE `an injury caused the death` TRUE `at a mine` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `any coroner who considers the death reportable (s 11(2)), or the coroner the State Coroner directs (s 11(3))`
#ASSERT `Which coroner investigates question` TRUE `an injury contributed to the death, but the person would have died anyway` TRUE `at a coal mine` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `any coroner who considers the death reportable (s 11(2)), or the coroner the State Coroner directs (s 11(3))`
#ASSERT `Which coroner investigates question` TRUE `an injury caused the death` FALSE `at a coal mine` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `any coroner who considers the death reportable (s 11(2)), or the coroner the State Coroner directs (s 11(3))`
#ASSERT `Which coroner investigates question` TRUE `an injury caused the death` TRUE `somewhere else` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `any coroner who considers the death reportable (s 11(2)), or the coroner the State Coroner directs (s 11(3))`
-- An unnatural death in custody, and one in a police pursuit: only the senior coroners (s 11(7)).
#ASSERT `Which coroner investigates question` TRUE `no injury played a part` FALSE `somewhere else` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `only the State Coroner, a Deputy State Coroner or a coroner approved by the Governor in Council (s 11(7))`
#ASSERT `Which coroner investigates question` TRUE `an injury caused the death` FALSE `somewhere else` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `only the State Coroner, a Deputy State Coroner or a coroner approved by the Governor in Council (s 11(7))`
-- A natural death in custody is not within s 11(7).
#ASSERT `Which coroner investigates question` FALSE `no injury played a part` FALSE `somewhere else` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `any coroner who considers the death reportable (s 11(2)), or the coroner the State Coroner directs (s 11(3))`
-- A prisoner on a work party killed at a mine: s 11AAA taken first (fork F2).
#ASSERT `Which coroner investigates question` TRUE `an injury caused the death` TRUE `at a mine` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `the Mining and Resources Coroner, or if that coroner is not available another coroner the State Coroner directs (s 11AAA(1))`

§ `s 11A -- challenging the reportability decision`

#ASSERT `Can I challenge the reportability decision question` `a coroner other than the State Coroner decided` (`dmy` 1 3 2027) (`dmy` 1 9 2027) EQUALS `yes: apply to the State Coroner (s 11A(2)(a)); s 11A sets no time limit`
#ASSERT `Can I challenge the reportability decision question` `the State Coroner decided, as the investigating coroner` (`dmy` 1 3 2027) (`dmy` 1 9 2027) EQUALS `yes: apply to the District Court (s 11A(2)(b)); s 11A sets no time limit for this application`
-- Reasons received 1 March 2027: the 14th day after is 15 March (in time); 16 March is late; the same day is in time.
#ASSERT `Can I challenge the reportability decision question` `the State Coroner decided my application for review of another coroner's decision` (`dmy` 1 3 2027) (`dmy` 15 3 2027) EQUALS `yes: apply to the District Court within 14 days after you receive the State Coroner's written reasons (s 11A(3), (4)); you are within time`
#ASSERT `Can I challenge the reportability decision question` `the State Coroner decided my application for review of another coroner's decision` (`dmy` 1 3 2027) (`dmy` 16 3 2027) EQUALS `no: an application to the District Court after the State Coroner's decision must be made within 14 days after you receive the written reasons (s 11A(4)), and that period has ended`
#ASSERT `Can I challenge the reportability decision question` `the State Coroner decided my application for review of another coroner's decision` (`dmy` 1 3 2027) (`dmy` 1 3 2027) EQUALS `yes: apply to the District Court within 14 days after you receive the State Coroner's written reasons (s 11A(3), (4)); you are within time`
#ASSERT `Last day to apply to the District Court about reportability question` (`dmy` 1 3 2027) EQUALS `dmy` 15 3 2027
-- Across a year end, and across 29 February 2028.
#ASSERT `Last day to apply to the District Court about reportability question` (`dmy` 20 12 2026) EQUALS `dmy` 3 1 2027
#ASSERT `Last day to apply to the District Court about reportability question` (`dmy` 28 2 2028) EQUALS `dmy` 13 3 2028
